7. At this stage, I would like to refer to the decision of the Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Rajesh Ranjan Yadav @ Pappu Yadav Vs. CBI Through its Director, reported in (2007) 1 SCC 70, wherein,
the Apex Court has laid down that, while considering an application for regular bail, the Courts shall have to take into consideration the following aspects:
"(a) The nature of accusation and the severity of punishment in case of conviction and the nature of supporting evidence;
(b) Reasonable apprehension of tampering with the witness or apprehension of threat to the complainant;
(c) Prima facie satisfaction of the court in support of the charge;"
8.
